                <pb facs="0156" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg56"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 319.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prince Kung to Mr. Young</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-11"><hi rendition="#small-caps">November</hi> 11,
                            1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Informal.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: In the matter of the pillage of
                    Shameen by the Cantonese, the Chinese Government propose to nominate a gentleman
                    to deal with it, and it becomes my duty to request the repersentatives of the
                    several Governments interested to consult together and name a gentleman to
                    arrange matters with the nominee of this Government. The two persons thus
                    appointed should choose a third person as referee, in order to avoid
                    controversy.</p>
                <p>It is my duty to request your excellency to notify this office of the person whom
                    you may see fit to nominate, and upon receipt of this information the name of
                    the nominee of this Government will be communicated to your excellency.</p>
                <p>Cards and compliments.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
